r-field/id #uuid "eff5306d-9491-5173-8aa7-74b8cd6d3205" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061122}] :question/id #uuid "7d711ed3-d6d7-5c91-92e6-31217e529094" :question/math-academy-id "q-12493" :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int(x - 2)^{10}dx$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79e1e950-d4fa-5802-a740-9f349f5e2bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245388} {:answer/id #uuid "a29e19f6-b9f6-59f0-a467-6fefa7b66ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245767} {:answer/id #uuid "a906b768-5358-5e2c-ba8d-6fb543703eed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245823} {:answer/id #uuid "f15bdc25-a157-589e-8f5a-8151a8371a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246444} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7b45bc-963d-5b75-90cd-534a19df4dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe7b45bc-963d-5b75-90cd-534a19df4dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246540} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a68bc5e-3ec4-5e14-bd3f-0dd750983f99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246566}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b3a2c849-8914-5088-a188-98bfa5cab912" :question/math-academy-id "q-113486" :question/problem "$\\int 48(3x-2)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3x-2.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 48(3x-2)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 48{u}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =2\\cdot {u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =2(3x-2)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-2)^{8}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-2)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =16(3x-2)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-2)+0 \\\\  & =16(3x-2)^{7}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =48(3x-2)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76cedac8-895d-5870-9926-547142cb0878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245369} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb3d7f9-74fd-5833-830c-4bb663c58640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245406} {:answer/id #uuid "9c74adb4-1a2f-50e8-94b8-808066441c8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245702} {:answer/id #uuid "9d96ffde-3b7c-59c4-81a4-cea06efe1c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245718} {:answer/id #uuid "d49f4656-7b64-54df-bf20-328340180875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d96ffde-3b7c-59c4-81a4-cea06efe1c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245718} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfc4b084-cb82-5c30-a425-7b47c8dea13e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246893}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b151b1a4-88b3-56e5-8da5-20d1f21f5f65" :question/math-academy-id "q-113492" :question/problem "$\\int 6(5-3x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=5-3x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6(5-3x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{u}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-2(5-3x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-3x)+0 \\\\  & =-2(5-3x)^{2}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6(5-3x)^{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247358 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33cd6666-68ef-5587-af38-937538b7c7d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244778} {:answer/id #uuid "a23e3f18-ccf0-5edd-90a9-074f7bdc257a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245761} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a116a5-5195-5bb5-8d8f-c3d5bdb58287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245768} {:answer/id #uuid "adf08c69-5710-5d54-9609-99700fa1b4c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245866} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf80ff9-edcb-547d-a18d-0ec0592f5a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdf80ff9-edcb-547d-a18d-0ec0592f5a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246151} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e9dc6ab-32fe-57ad-a8b7-97d5999f7994" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246714}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4aa132c6-373a-5f63-a95e-dc8b634b917a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113503" :question/problem "$\\int 9(3-2x)^{8}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3-2x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9(3-2x)^{8}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 9{u}^{8}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\int {u}^{8}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}\\int {u}^{8}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{9}}{9}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{9}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}(3-2x)^{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3-2x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}(3-2x)^{8}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =9(3-2x)^{8}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398102 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "326be129-c932-54e7-bd6e-d61f8a6c1750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398104} {:answer/id #uuid "d8f6915c-a30b-538c-be4c-c5d4feafc456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398105} {:answer/id #uuid "d929af17-b6b6-5bb1-9948-38e8c5714648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398106} {:answer/id #uuid "e257789f-7b07-5075-adc9-57e60483dc0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398107} {:answer/id #uuid "65143245-b12a-5ed5-a1a3-dc55de2b261a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8f6915c-a30b-538c-be4c-c5d4feafc456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398105} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d582062-813e-5b4d-b116-6b4cb9d5d390" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398103}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "201b1303-edfe-5a94-b70a-3687fd03d284" :question/math-academy-id "q-113502" :question/problem "$\\int 18(2-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2-5x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 18(2-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 18{u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =18\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\int {u}^{5}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{u}^{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2-5x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{5}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =18(2-5x)^{5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6058cb14-4722-5ae2-982a-1d1d72759305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398963} {:answer/id #uuid "615ab3c3-1cc9-56db-a561-9ade7641ace4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398964} {:answer/id #uuid "2b200597-1f86-5ecd-b8bc-18b09c132aad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398965} {:answer/id #uuid "13a3fa38-b420-5956-8a4b-2194f2d8ef30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398966} {:answer/id #uuid "5674f007-df38-5b04-ac90-1342c70182a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6058cb14-4722-5ae2-982a-1d1d72759305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398963} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee57767-a470-5ed2-888e-e7479cb9accb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398962}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c75bb9c-44e2-5f73-9a68-3c296ae237a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72424" :question/problem "$\\int 16(7-2x)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=7-2x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 16(7-2x)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 16{u}^{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\int {u}^{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =-{u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =-(7-2x)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-(7-2x)^{8}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(7-2x)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-8(7-2x)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-2x)+0 \\\\  & =-8(7-2x)^{7}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =16(7-2x)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7377f12f-bbc8-5b20-aa7a-f0707a87a5ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16(3x-7)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485725} {:answer/id #uuid "77281a58-3d49-5fd8-a3b1-1af350ca3499" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(3x-7)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485726} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed06ac1-fd5a-51e5-a93c-e84caa88a78a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8(3x-7)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485730} {:answer/id #uuid "9f78c7e8-599a-56d5-9dae-9aea344e3c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-7)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485732} {:answer/id #uuid "be5bbccf-1a6d-5e2d-9e42-d65a07463850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(3x-7)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f78c7e8-599a-56d5-9dae-9aea344e3c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-7)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485732} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa23e206-e2c7-5918-8bd9-348e98fbec24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485734}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22ca9ca5-3802-5b5f-8227-216a5d3cf02e" :question/problem "$\\int 48(3x-7)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3x-7.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 48(3x-7)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 48{u}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =2\\cdot {u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =2(3x-7)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-7)^{8}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-7)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =16(3x-7)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-7)+0 \\\\  & =16(3x-7)^{7}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =48(3x-7)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485721 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a9f23ca-cacc-5e1e-abb5-55c7d3a45c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-13)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485713} {:answer/id #uuid "20d2ad2c-fb89-58a7-8091-651be6dd4bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16(3x-13)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485715} {:answer/id #uuid "376db25a-fc5f-5042-8c89-64bba6c97f11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8(3x-13)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485718} {:answer/id #uuid "44984ed3-c9b5-5cf7-8d1e-15b7fd85d79d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(3x-13)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485719} {:answer/id #uuid "f75603bf-fe81-50c1-9321-dc5b1249a827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(3x-13)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a9f23ca-cacc-5e1e-abb5-55c7d3a45c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-13)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485713} :answer-field/id #uuid "839b108c-5fff-581b-9e63-b66af5e351b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485728}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45e3bd8b-7650-5cda-96ec-8c1136f22506" :question/problem "$\\int 48(3x-13)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3x-13.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 48(3x-13)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 48{u}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =2\\cdot {u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =2(3x-13)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-13)^{8}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-13)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =16(3x-13)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-13)+0 \\\\  & =16(3x-13)^{7}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =48(3x-13)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45e0f19a-f9d5-5228-9b94-58ecab8e87eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485720} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2f5002-2107-58c8-b0a8-882b075d5cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485722} {:answer/id #uuid "a493d69f-2007-5ffc-875a-4c2592acbcbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485733} {:answer/id #uuid "be12a189-8ba2-5094-a4bd-2c96645a1c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485737} {:answer/id #uuid "e88c3d26-48cf-5e5e-aeb6-17a6ad386592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a493d69f-2007-5ffc-875a-4c2592acbcbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485733} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcc87777-afa0-5b4d-9e7c-63b17177db48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485745}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8858620f-52c4-55a0-8eb8-6d919612e467" :question/problem "$\\int 18(12-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=12-5x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 18(12-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 18{u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =18\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\int {u}^{5}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{u}^{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{3}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{3}{5}(12-5x)^{6}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(12-5x)^{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12-5x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(12-5x)^{5}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =18(12-5x)^{5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bed476f-b17b-51bc-a0cd-c606ea7fc94d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(3x-3)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485714} {:answer/id #uuid "69447685-2199-54a6-8884-7121ab8e8b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(3x-3)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485724} {:answer/id #uuid "941acafa-f15d-5838-ae68-bc7c6834a2ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16(3x-3)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485731} {:answer/id #uuid "bb923d54-7741-53b9-97a9-ae6d17fefaea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8(3x-3)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485736} {:answer/id #uuid "ed546a36-da04-5b10-afcd-713ccfc4f479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-3)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed546a36-da04-5b10-afcd-713ccfc4f479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-3)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485743} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e794a0a-3082-5da9-8a0e-f71bd5273e3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485723}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7b871d9-2b64-5d5f-980a-acf58621c326" :question/problem "$\\int 48(3x-3)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3x-3.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 48(3x-3)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 48{u}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =2\\cdot {u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =2(3x-3)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-3)^{8}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-3)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =16(3x-3)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-3)+0 \\\\  & =16(3x-3)^{7}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =48(3x-3)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485746 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c3f877-a893-5024-bb8c-047db29a33f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8(3x-1)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485712} {:answer/id #uuid "27297270-ed6e-5a77-b95c-b94f11821c79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(3x-1)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485717} {:answer/id #uuid "7ae58990-6a59-5ad7-a808-52a7616ed5e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16(3x-1)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485727} {:answer/id #uuid "ac265dc5-84e4-5ff4-ac5a-405b42e5e55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-1)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485735} {:answer/id #uuid "e7cf2218-e43e-5b62-a006-74ce1a683da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(3x-1)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac265dc5-84e4-5ff4-ac5a-405b42e5e55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-1)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485735} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9b7264f-8376-5ba7-ab8c-5dd4567f8df3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485742}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd40cdc2-bda1-52a5-ab17-92f594c6d05e" :question/problem "$\\int 48(3x-1)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3x-1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 48(3x-1)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 48{u}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =2\\cdot {u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =2(3x-1)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-1)^{8}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-1)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =16(3x-1)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-1)+0 \\\\  & =16(3x-1)^{7}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =48(3x-1)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Positive Integer Exponent"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064204 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064072 :question/id #uuid "e469c042-9619-55d4-b745-d4ed26251d80" :question/math-academy-id "e-447" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2}{(1-x)^3} \\,  \\textrm{d}x .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int 2(1-x)^{-3} \\,  \\textrm{d}x .\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x =  -\\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2(1-x)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{u}^{-3}\\cdot (-1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\int {u}^{-3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{-2}}{-2}+C \\\\  & ={u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =(1-x)^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(1-x)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-2(1-x)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1-x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(1-x)^{3}}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(1-x)^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "387d85df-b839-5837-89b9-5e4bb4daa073" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064480 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2295f789-3426-5c13-8072-48ad046a0397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(1-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250848} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4cefaf-cc26-5de6-9514-472253277759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3(1-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250939} {:answer/id #uuid "7672b2ad-aa8f-5d9b-b569-2cc387ccbabd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(1-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251527} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2f7df9-5402-574e-adb2-2561ceb6b638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2(1-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252072} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e85065-6ff4-5195-b17d-22aae81082ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(1-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2295f789-3426-5c13-8072-48ad046a0397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(1-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250848} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0d653fa-fe23-5a9d-871d-2b6ab43cc543" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253188}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff0caf62-efde-5e81-b5d3-dad00511c8fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-12019" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3}{(1-3x)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 3(1-3x)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-3x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3(1-3x)^{-3} & =3\\int {u}^{-3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(-2)}{u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-3x)^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(1-3x)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{2(1-3x)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(1-3x)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(1-3x)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)(1-3x)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1-3x)+0 \\\\  & =-(1-3x)^{-3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =3(1-3x)^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(1-3x)^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064483 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9923461c-ea68-5de4-a7c2-f232c840755f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (1)/(7(x - 3)^{7}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061129} {:answer/id #uuid "a4dcfa8f-e3b7-5a31-89ee-98229564c8d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(7(x - 3)^{7}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061130} {:answer/id #uuid "e6bb9196-85e7-5244-8445-64c44a66da55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (1)/(7(x - 3)^{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061131} {:answer/id #uuid "5559a580-51a5-5468-9dd1-981105cf44fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(9(x - 3)^{9})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061132} {:answer/id #uuid "584255b1-754c-5fca-84ba-405b71b03c2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(9(x - 3)^{9}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061133}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ebeb1770-1d40-5b41-a8d0-c510eeac6052" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061128}] :question/id #uuid "fe72e74d-a333-5131-976a-24546ffabb73" :question/math-academy-id "q-12499" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int(1)/((x - 3)^{8})dx$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bc5c6fd-bdf8-52fc-bcc8-34f34365280e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5(5x-1)^{7}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244989} {:answer/id #uuid "637d4b9b-93b2-5844-95c0-865fb0d8d6a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{35(5x-1)^{7}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245185} {:answer/id #uuid "a45fab6e-368a-5f8f-a84b-7e25d8888d84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5(5x-1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245784} {:answer/id #uuid "a986c32b-070a-5fc6-b027-801d97880cf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245826} {:answer/id #uuid "b410e874-f38e-56b0-a2b2-4bb2712e9ff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a986c32b-070a-5fc6-b027-801d97880cf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245826} :answer-field/id #uuid "865ffc4d-f1ea-5522-81fb-9f6d4c054a35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246780}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a85bee8-3587-5c69-bd5f-2ededc7e8236" :question/math-academy-id "q-113511" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{(5x-1)^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (5x-1)^{-6}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5x-1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5x-1)^{-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{-6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{-6}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5}){u}^{-5}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{25{u}^{5}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{25}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(5x-1)^{-5}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{25}\\cdot (-5)\\cdot (5x-1)^{-6}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x-1)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5(5x-1)^{6}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(5x-1)^{6}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247361 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "256fd45e-791f-579f-8818-27b200a5be2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6(2x+3)^{6}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244646} {:answer/id #uuid "5af7f51f-ec62-58f7-bebf-0a5e46ab25ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245108} {:answer/id #uuid "86b0dab8-9a9c-5dc1-898f-16713fd82cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245500} {:answer/id #uuid "ba397c98-9bb5-5539-8012-42dae1cdb3ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{16(2x+3)^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245977} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bc3d02-224b-549e-92f2-90a5f845c0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(2x+3)^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b0dab8-9a9c-5dc1-898f-16713fd82cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245500} :answer-field/id #uuid "082ed3b9-9437-5ec7-963d-859b2b91ef1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246564}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "094b9ad8-d309-510f-9910-b086cac9a8d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-113512" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{(2x+3)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (2x+3)^{-7}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2x+3.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+3)^{-7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{-7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{-7}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{6}){u}^{-6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12{u}^{6}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(2x+3)^{-6}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot (-6)\\cdot (2x+3)^{-7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+3)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(2x+3)^{7}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(2x+3)^{7}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee252b3-2fc9-58a1-a526-0ad834b9b6a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250686} {:answer/id #uuid "18391112-3f3a-57a1-9bfe-ef48a937491a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250766} {:answer/id #uuid "1e9cae62-9c68-5e87-9549-65a72091d03a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250813} {:answer/id #uuid "405c4f12-0925-5899-8b0c-bf237460ec93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251088} {:answer/id #uuid "988c1baf-6f97-581c-b7f2-f8c57f43988e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "988c1baf-6f97-581c-b7f2-f8c57f43988e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251863} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae027c21-9aa0-573c-bcf0-1d5cd80234b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253108}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03a455ba-2873-5368-831e-308d6a1a251d" :question/math-academy-id "q-12018" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{6}{(2x-3)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 6(2x-3)^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2x-3.$Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6(2x-3)^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{u}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3}){u}^{-3}+C \\\\  & =-{u}^{-3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(2x-3)^{-3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-(-3)\\cdot (2x-3)^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-3)+0 \\\\  & =3\\cdot (2x-3)^{-4}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(2x-3)^{4}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a0d85b8-3324-57f7-a467-f401be804083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(5x-7)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336578} {:answer/id #uuid "75e6122b-2104-52f4-b814-dae601247c06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{(5x-7)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337093} {:answer/id #uuid "8b91db05-c595-568e-b4ad-f97b5c3c6882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(5x-7)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337295} {:answer/id #uuid "aaed332c-7186-53b8-802e-6557581b75af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{(5x-7)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337573} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ae619c-f25b-53f5-8b0f-30595a2ff518" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{(5x-7)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a0d85b8-3324-57f7-a467-f401be804083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(5x-7)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336578} :answer-field/id #uuid "eda4e982-7475-54c5-abfe-c6e946514b7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338692}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5692ce6-f75c-5a26-9487-0e066184decc" :question/math-academy-id "q-72429" :question/problem "$\\int -\\frac{15}{(5x-7)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int -15(5x-7)^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5x-7.$Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -15(5x-7)^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -15{u}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-3\\int {u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3}){u}^{-3}+C \\\\  & ={u}^{-3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(5x-7)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(5x-7)^{3}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(5x-7)^{3}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(5x-7)^{-3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (5x-7)^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x-7)+0 \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (5x-7)^{-4}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{(5x-7)^{4}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09c396ba-d664-5b85-8ba8-8e75dd8fbd90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336119} {:answer/id #uuid "0db6811e-089b-562c-ba27-284a4fd3ea8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336160} {:answer/id #uuid "28d420b6-69c3-5606-bbbb-988485d9f4f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336414} {:answer/id #uuid "770e9c77-7b33-5f86-84b2-1c73fd57475c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337104} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7a1e25-6e8c-5f9b-b884-a307ed2ee9c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09c396ba-d664-5b85-8ba8-8e75dd8fbd90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336119} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a548983-c429-59e9-a111-6bd915ce2c3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338492}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e19e6ed6-2d0f-56db-a2d1-ee7e2496cc04" :question/math-academy-id "q-72431" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{4}{(8-x)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 4(8-x)^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=8-x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4(8-x)^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int {u}^{-5}\\cdot (-1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)\\int {u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\int {u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{(-4)}{u}^{-4}+C \\\\  & =(8-x)^{-4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(8-x)^{-4}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =(-4)(8-x)^{-5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8-x)+0 \\\\  & =(-4)(8-x)^{-5}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4(8-x)^{-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(8-x)^{5}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87bb5e34-8a7e-5077-9056-44171c31d68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398111} {:answer/id #uuid "73df82c1-76f6-50ea-99b9-53a33ba7607d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398112} {:answer/id #uuid "cfab3df7-4bb6-5eeb-9342-3841991827b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398113} {:answer/id #uuid "1e49762e-1e14-5248-8c9e-16a5e673bda1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398114} {:answer/id #uuid "15a56691-9975-5ae2-aa7b-fda010fe63b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15a56691-9975-5ae2-aa7b-fda010fe63b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398115} :answer-field/id #uuid "c13dea0f-f218-5cd2-a503-c7b2250d51fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398110}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1948aa2d-5fbb-59f5-8ccc-6dd9cfd6ef51" :question/math-academy-id "q-113509" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (x-2)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=x-2.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x-2)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{-3}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{u}^{2}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(x-2)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (x-2)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x-2)+0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06f0d601-5b9e-5b34-b1e4-35332ff61132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20(9-5x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398118} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0f063f-eba9-55db-a617-104bbe47e493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398119} {:answer/id #uuid "199a03cb-71ce-557c-b3af-135bd3564f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398120} {:answer/id #uuid "418bd3f4-e4c0-5bc7-b4ac-5541696af9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398121} {:answer/id #uuid "51978e0d-c725-5111-8fd8-58bfe89fa4d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "418bd3f4-e4c0-5bc7-b4ac-5541696af9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398121} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b49b60e-8217-5844-bea9-fe48c12aaf25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398117}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d34fadec-e1db-5f0e-b3fb-64f3326f1376" :question/math-academy-id "q-113517" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{(9-5x)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (9-5x)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=9-5x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (9-5x)^{-3}\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{-3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}){u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10{u}^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(9-5x)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot (-2)(9-5x)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9-5x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}(9-5x)^{-3}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =(9-5x)^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(9-5x)}^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483548 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0299ebf8-922a-55f9-979e-c5b2750f2024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3(5-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483540} {:answer/id #uuid "546c1b82-6a06-546c-a3a1-9a01e9e99c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(5-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483544} {:answer/id #uuid "6a17550f-8b1e-5076-b4f3-14f620872486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2(5-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483546} {:answer/id #uuid "ca795e82-112a-5ece-bd1d-9787baea0287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(5-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483550} {:answer/id #uuid "e443c9d7-7721-59f8-a709-03552a1eb4bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(5-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca795e82-112a-5ece-bd1d-9787baea0287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(5-3x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483550} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbbfcc56-2097-59e6-8df3-eab502cf4f79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483551}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8425667-976e-5474-9182-8785229638c8" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3}{(5-3x)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 3(5-3x)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5-3x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3(5-3x)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int {u}^{-3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(-2)}{u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(5-3x)^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(5-3x)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{2(5-3x)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(5-3x)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(5-3x)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)(5-3x)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-3x)+0 \\\\  & =-(5-3x)^{-3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =3(5-3x)^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(5-3x)^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483549 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1360a76d-bdc7-5f69-b60a-bd2f09ca9f84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(3-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483541} {:answer/id #uuid "269e93ad-dc56-5ae8-9082-a55eb20287dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{(3-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483542} {:answer/id #uuid "40e2a044-06da-5da0-8f33-77eb00e3d1ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(3-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483543} {:answer/id #uuid "5b96278e-eb56-5e2c-8b74-597a29b2b2a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(3-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483545} {:answer/id #uuid "a0336689-0e13-5f83-9272-b3409590e5d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(3-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1360a76d-bdc7-5f69-b60a-bd2f09ca9f84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(3-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483541} :answer-field/id #uuid "f44b9ca1-9b1d-5e25-9550-150b2f5c324d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483553}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "beed05dd-1df0-5509-b310-7367b8962226" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{4}{(3-x)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 4(3-x)^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3-x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4(3-x)^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int {u}^{-5}\\cdot (-1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)\\int {u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\int {u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{(-4)}{u}^{-4}+C \\\\  & =(3-x)^{-4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(3-x)^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(3-x)^{4}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(3-x)^{4}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(3-x)^{-4}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =(-4)(3-x)^{-5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3-x)+0 \\\\  & =(-4)(3-x)^{-5}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4(3-x)^{-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(3-x)^{5}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Negative Integer Exponent"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064205 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064075 :question/id #uuid "e416cb5c-22df-55e4-a3cb-c6b5dfc650c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-448" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int\\sqrt{1-5x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int(1-5x)^{1/2}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=1-5x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 5 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-5x)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{1/2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{15}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{15}(1-5x)^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(1-5x)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(1-5x)^{3}}+C] & =-\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\sqrt{(1-5x)^{3}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(1-5x)^{3/2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(1-5x)^{1/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1-5x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}(1-5x)^{1/2}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =(1-5x)^{1/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19d524de-41c3-5692-80f8-9a4d0dcb4194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y-1}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330173} {:answer/id #uuid "31e39ca9-2857-5b87-84c3-073fed26c8f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y-1}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330386} {:answer/id #uuid "3e6afaa1-40a2-5f9d-b8a6-55b54cd316ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y-1}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330504} {:answer/id #uuid "764b6e79-b531-58f5-bebf-0d23607d95b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{4y-1}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331009} {:answer/id #uuid "894f060c-93b0-58ae-b0f2-ccf91e5072db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{4y-1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19d524de-41c3-5692-80f8-9a4d0dcb4194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y-1}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330173} :answer-field/id #uuid "5934f87d-cda7-5062-8b5d-25163acd381a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332372}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c4056b3-c70d-593e-9370-73ee76b66f6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49391" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4y-1}}\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (4y-1)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=4y-1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $y$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}y=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4y-1)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(1/2)}{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{4}\\cdot {u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4y-1)^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4y-1}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[\\frac{\\sqrt{4y-1}}{2}+C] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[\\sqrt{4y-1}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[(4y-1)^{1/2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(4y-1)^{-1/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(4y-1)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(4y-1)^{-1/2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4y-1}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c16d112-7916-5db7-92cb-ea050cfa86c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{7}\\sqrt[4]{(1 - z)^{7}} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063229} {:answer/id #uuid "b42189aa-3510-533d-804b-03f153598c79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt[3]{(1 - z)^{7}} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063230} {:answer/id #uuid "dd3c477e-24f0-5406-be4c-5192a3640ac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sqrt[3]{(1 - z)^{7}} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063231} {:answer/id #uuid "0dadbfcd-c66a-5aab-a6f2-04e5739fd0e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sqrt[4]{(1 - z)^{7}} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063232} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4a4416-9652-5d2d-9967-8849fb093f05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[4]{(1 - z)^{7}} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063233}] :answer-field/id #uuid "41a3a7d4-7f43-573e-9173-8db117067921" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063228}] :question/id #uuid "74ddc3f6-85cd-5a53-9654-1fbca7eb8497" :question/math-academy-id "q-49392" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int\\sqrt[4]{(1 - z)^{3}}dz$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05dc1d0c-6562-5063-8b6a-fb2761a7610a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281740} {:answer/id #uuid "2c23b35a-058b-5db4-9003-d4cc23104b44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{20}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282078} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6123f8-d142-5770-8b49-a723c5b081c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282484} {:answer/id #uuid "815ab18e-3bdc-566d-897a-290bc02c3418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282802} {:answer/id #uuid "cccc287f-7075-53df-994c-57ed770387d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{20}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c23b35a-058b-5db4-9003-d4cc23104b44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{20}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282078} :answer-field/id #uuid "0de7d9ff-8de4-57f9-8a25-279d79c35b36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283960}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "17ae717b-d689-565d-9092-d0ded31ed5c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-17019" :question/problem "Calculate the integral\n$\\int \\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (3-4x)^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we let  $u=3-4x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3-4x)^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{2/3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5/3}{u}^{5/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}{u}^{5/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{20}{u}^{5/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{20}(3-4x)^{5/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{20}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{3}{20}(3-4x)^{5/3}+C] & =-\\frac{3}{20}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(3-4x)^{5/3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{20}\\cdot \\frac{5}{3}(3-4x)^{2/3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3-4x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(3-4x)^{3/2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =(3-4x)^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{2}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c11ff0-71d5-5bee-aae5-8b0816d61754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330128} {:answer/id #uuid "5f2cfdeb-9842-58b1-b828-74e45464f343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3\\sqrt[4]{1-5s}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330797} {:answer/id #uuid "61a59c95-07ff-5f5f-971c-f9bd9ea7288e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{7}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330822} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6dd38f-46e2-5f77-9d50-cb6ab9cd68d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331062} {:answer/id #uuid "c7305939-90b2-595f-b633-babd5a276440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e6dd38f-46e2-5f77-9d50-cb6ab9cd68d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331062} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f47b77-e5fb-5327-8f5a-bf4eb1d0b728" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332635}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "44b08892-d784-5133-8162-d9d2c70e3c9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-49393" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{(3-5s)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}s=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (3-5s)^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNow, we let  $u=3-5s.$ Then differentiating with respect to $s$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}s}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}s=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3-5s)^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}s & =\\int {u}^{-2/3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1/3}{u}^{1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{u}^{1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}(3-5s)^{1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C] & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[(3-5s)^{1/3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}(3-5s)^{-2/3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3-5s)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}(3-5s)^{-2/3}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =(3-5s)^{-2/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{(3-5s)^{2}}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332715 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e3acb8a-9c64-589a-b0a1-55d19079df04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330356} {:answer/id #uuid "4a84cb98-9b13-5e1d-b3f0-776b95159569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330622} {:answer/id #uuid "82c50580-ea5f-5d76-a971-e5772b6896c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331107} {:answer/id #uuid "9807ff7c-bea9-5fb1-8910-b8a4f9e1bd42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331305} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ceaa5d-7317-520f-bbe3-4033344e9924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9807ff7c-bea9-5fb1-8910-b8a4f9e1bd42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331305} :answer-field/id #uuid "1efac576-99bc-59ee-aebb-307554ed47c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332246}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dab90c5a-327c-5636-bfaa-e6da096f9912" :question/math-academy-id "q-49437" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (y+11)^{5/3}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=y+11.$ Then differentiating with respect to $y$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}y=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (y+11)^{5/3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {u}^{5/3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{8/3}}{8/3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}(y+11)^{8/3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{8}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[\\frac{3}{8}\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{8}}] & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{8}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[(y+11)^{8/3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}(y+11)^{5/3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+11)+0 \\\\  & =(y+11)^{5/3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{(y+11)^{5}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c00a40ba-01e3-5ee1-8e78-5ca100de2c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395730} {:answer/id #uuid "b95804dd-01ed-5465-b1ec-454869fcea4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{5x+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395731} {:answer/id #uuid "957bc594-a52d-54c5-8fe2-348b94cdf190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{5x+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395732} {:answer/id #uuid "40a36a09-4403-51a9-8c9b-14cdbfe2aa41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395733} {:answer/id #uuid "2458c64b-d709-5fd5-a6bf-7d12e7bb36e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40a36a09-4403-51a9-8c9b-14cdbfe2aa41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395733} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bf9bf65-124a-5233-aedc-81c57617266f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395729}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "457b9ae0-36a8-577c-85ad-8057dc66fc9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-12498" :question/problem "$\\int \\sqrt{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (5x+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=5x+1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5x+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{1/2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}(5x+1)^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C] & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(5x+1)^{3/2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(5x+1)^{1/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x+1)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(5x+1)^{1/2}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =(5x+1)^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5x+1}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398869 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739b7d37-465f-53a0-92fd-a46f218e891c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{(1-9z)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398871} {:answer/id #uuid "c966cc5b-2f5d-56fa-94a2-562519ed3dc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{1-9z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398872} {:answer/id #uuid "570962e4-656c-562b-b969-b8505698bd15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{1-9z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398873} {:answer/id #uuid "bede226b-b6b5-5601-a51f-99f2392a59d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{1-9z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398874} {:answer/id #uuid "c91eab72-8ce7-50be-b8c3-3258720d8056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{(1-9z)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "570962e4-656c-562b-b969-b8505698bd15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{1-9z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398873} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1f41607-89e1-5a62-888e-441db9b42ea9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398870}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78d0396e-82eb-542b-a43f-b6df87f217ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-49431" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-9z}}\\,\\text{d}z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (1-9z)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=1-9z.$ Then differentiating with respect to $z$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}=-9\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}z=-\\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-9z)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\frac{1}{(1/2)}{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}(1-9z)^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{1-9z}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}[-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{1-9z}+C] & =-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}[\\sqrt{1-9z}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}[(1-9z)^{1/2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1-9z)^{-1/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(1-9z)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (1-9z)^{-1/2}\\cdot (-9) \\\\  & =(1-9z)^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-9z}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70657675-2db0-5a10-9cf9-052f05edf016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{11}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398878} {:answer/id #uuid "3909aff4-3810-5b83-850f-f988be7ba4f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398879} {:answer/id #uuid "4061afb3-02dc-5f4e-ae19-437ea14959c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398880} {:answer/id #uuid "3295113f-e7ef-59d3-92a7-66e977a1b12b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{9}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398881} {:answer/id #uuid "732c775a-c5f4-5d4e-91c3-0fdfab8cfb52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{9}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70657675-2db0-5a10-9cf9-052f05edf016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{11}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398878} :answer-field/id #uuid "cad56171-faf0-523d-b089-53ed18731d86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398877}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61d8dd43-99c6-5162-9111-9fc96bb88dcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-49439" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (x-100)^{7/4}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we let  $u=x-100.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x-100)^{7/4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{7/4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{11/4}}{11/4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{11}(x-100)^{11/4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{11}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{4}{11}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C] & =\\frac{4}{11}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{11}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(x-100)^{11/4}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{11}\\cdot \\frac{11}{4}(x-100)^{7/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x-100)+0 \\\\  & =(x-100)^{7/4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{7}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398883 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64f1bb19-f6a2-538a-8094-300b1e55cc31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398885} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8f42a5-cc05-5072-93b3-0b55ad819b57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398886} {:answer/id #uuid "1c531862-1246-5d33-83db-faf2c5f53bfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398887} {:answer/id #uuid "eeef3e88-28df-595f-88f1-2280a46131c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398888} {:answer/id #uuid "c04d34f3-85b9-5e8c-b8f6-dc61a84a62ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c04d34f3-85b9-5e8c-b8f6-dc61a84a62ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398889} :answer-field/id #uuid "69629315-77cc-510c-b6be-75d926e5d966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398884}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2058ea27-d95b-5f37-8b22-5c724bfe6f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-49468" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}s=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {(s+1)}^{-3/5}\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNow, we let  $u=s+1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $s$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}s}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}s=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(s+1)}^{-3/5}\\,\\text{d}s & =\\int {u}^{-3/5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2/5}{u}^{2/5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{u}^{2/5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{(s+1)}^{2/5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[{(s+1)}^{2/5}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{(s+1)}^{-3/5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s+1)+0 \\\\  & ={(s+1)}^{-3/5}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{3}}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484773 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bc1f79d-9230-53d0-94a1-8d0212d70804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{-9-9z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484776} {:answer/id #uuid "6b37e588-2985-50e0-b7f6-7cb598fa2168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{-9-9z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484778} {:answer/id #uuid "81cb5d78-ddc4-5567-b381-5ebc30345f71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{(-9-9z)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484779} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef53196-4f93-51cf-a11f-980d673f4584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{(-9-9z)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484782} {:answer/id #uuid "fb202966-738f-50e3-aa47-63ef143a8d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{-9-9z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b37e588-2985-50e0-b7f6-7cb598fa2168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{-9-9z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484778} :answer-field/id #uuid "fac9a634-5a81-5ebd-9608-fc528d18a3ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484785}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d18d6d6-4996-55a3-8a5c-e103e6790f83" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-9-9z}}\\,\\text{d}z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (-9-9z)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=-9-9z.$ Then differentiating with respect to $z$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}=-9\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}z=-\\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $z$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (-9-9z)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\frac{1}{(1/2)}{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}(-9-9z)^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{-9-9z}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}[-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{-9-9z}+C] & =-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}[\\sqrt{-9-9z}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}[(-9-9z)^{1/2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(-9-9z)^{-1/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(-9-9z)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (-9-9z)^{-1/2}\\cdot (-9) \\\\  & =(-9-9z)^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-9-9z}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a0fde4-6c24-58e7-8907-6d8654047db1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(5x-50)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484774} {:answer/id #uuid "395ccb33-f39e-5064-b2d3-f2afb52894fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x-50)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484775} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1f2e80-7a1d-5bc0-972b-78c0f2b50e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{5x-50}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484777} {:answer/id #uuid "83ae88bd-f536-5748-bae2-ac5ea45c189e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{5x-50}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484780} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f20b17-9941-5017-867c-b8aa88c58c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(5x-50)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "395ccb33-f39e-5064-b2d3-f2afb52894fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x-50)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484775} :answer-field/id #uuid "c299197f-14a7-5515-95eb-0c4198b78e17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484783}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b9ac773-a814-5857-b454-ae543e57ffe1" :question/problem "$\\int \\sqrt{5x-50}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (5x-50)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=5x-50.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5x-50)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{1/2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}(5x-50)^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x-50)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x-50)^{3}}+C] & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\sqrt{(5x-50)^{3}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(5x-50)^{3/2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(5x-50)^{1/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x-50)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(5x-50)^{1/2}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =(5x-50)^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5x-50}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Fractional Exponent"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068724 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068566 :question/id #uuid "49f679c4-bbc4-59a5-9b0c-0f3b69d7cf57" :question/math-academy-id "e-454" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{x^2}{x^3+1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^3+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 3x^2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u= x^2 \\, \\textrm d x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+1}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}+1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "18ce1807-3a09-5ebd-b3cd-a91db8d2b4a8" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048557 :topic/math-academy-id 331 :topic/title "Integrating Linear Rational Functions Using Substitution"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89cbbcfc-00ad-53c7-b1e4-f74c30e23742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2)/((x^{2} - 1)^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065620} {:answer/id #uuid "b505fb8e-eba7-5140-a855-35f6a4f2675c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid x^{2} - 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065621} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e7b32b-88b1-5259-a368-fa1f163ed93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(2(x^{2} - 1)^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065622} {:answer/id #uuid "2dcf2fc8-01b2-5836-816b-2e75cf472f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\ln \\mid x^{2} - 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065623} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0c6e1d-f86b-5e04-a5b5-5f64b9b9d40d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid x^{2} - 1 \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065624}] :answer-field/id #uuid "aeff9a7e-466b-580e-a976-b234214756fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065619}] :question/id #uuid "fe887383-d000-50e4-b251-b388a44be6d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-12500" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{x}{x^{2} - 1}dx$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a56f775-026e-59fc-b647-34d85fe8bf61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3{x}^{2}-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336275} {:answer/id #uuid "a1728457-38ba-5bbb-927c-7282a90dc1b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337496} {:answer/id #uuid "b51f8e66-052a-5029-8ff7-97299bdc0642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}-x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337639} {:answer/id #uuid "f743a007-0c6c-5682-a772-447548f069d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3{x}^{2}-x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338200} {:answer/id #uuid "f9436168-b71c-5730-9e91-324b6cdb60f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-1}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b51f8e66-052a-5029-8ff7-97299bdc0642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}-x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337639} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9839270-94f7-5e94-999d-41a70f88e25f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338685}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "604f6b09-192e-50e6-8477-dce586313508" :question/math-academy-id "q-72566" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{3}-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{3}-x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=(3{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{3}-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-x}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}-x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0422cb62-0c61-58da-94f7-f0c7e04bc54f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{ln}(2{t}^{2}+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0422cb62-0c61-58da-94f7-f0c7e04bc54f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{ln}(2{t}^{2}+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234557} :answer-field/id #uuid "a27d93e9-cbea-537e-8fd4-f771273be507" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235169}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7449abb3-586b-5fd3-93e0-df3f3d5afa01" :question/math-academy-id "q-132982" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{-16t}{2{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t=\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,K.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2{t}^{2}+3.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=4t\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can solve the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-16t}{2{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t & =-16\\int \\frac{1}{2{t}^{2}+3}\\cdot t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-16\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+K \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{t}^{2}+3)+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c3e4e9-b986-5ba0-8bda-1e9028952e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x-{x}^{4}|}{1-4{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244505} {:answer/id #uuid "67d9c50b-eb65-5148-adba-2cc568ed70ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{1-4{x}^{3}}{1+x-{x}^{4}}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245232} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf0db7f-9d0d-5e1e-84fe-0e0a3ad04e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x-{x}^{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245270} {:answer/id #uuid "8f80e297-bea8-557a-a4d0-20991cf10a78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{1+x-{x}^{4}}{1-4{x}^{3}}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245565} {:answer/id #uuid "f01cc4c4-3137-5262-9a77-8fcd829c9bc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-4{x}^{3}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bf0db7f-9d0d-5e1e-84fe-0e0a3ad04e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x-{x}^{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245270} :answer-field/id #uuid "449306db-0c30-5468-98a1-e16f99561f62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246658}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5eb9147-51e3-5599-8ff3-2e89cfeea2e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-113719" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1-4{x}^{3}}{1+x-{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1+x-{x}^{4}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1-4{x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=(1-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1-4{x}^{3}}{1+x-{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+x-{x}^{4}}\\cdot (1-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x-{x}^{4}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/r